.TH UNBAN 10 "October 2026" "1.1" "Neverdark Manual"
.SH NAME
unban \- Lift a player's ban from a region
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unban
.I player
.RI [ region ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Lift
.IR player "'s"
ban from a region. You are told the ban is lifted, and the victim is told
they were unbanned. Banning nobody answers that the player is not banned
there.
.PP
The region is a bare world number (0\-65535) or the keyword \fBcosmos\fP,
under exactly the same rules as every other region selector. Without one the
command acts on your \fBdefault target region\fP (see \fBtarget\fP(10)), or
on the region you are standing in if you have set none. Regions at other
widths (districts, super\-planet regions \-\- see \fBgrant\fP(10)) are
reached through your default; see \fBtarget\fP(10) for the width\-and\-point
form.
.PP
The player who placed the ban, or anyone ruling the region now, may lift it:
a ban must not outlive the authority that could remove it, and a new ruler
must not be stuck with the old ruler's bans.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ban,target,here,planet (10)
.SH AUTHOR
quirinpa <quirinpa@tty.pt>
